Reach the quantized-embedding path on every architecture, in one place.

`VocabParallelEmbedding.__init__` only consults a quantization config if its
caller passed one, and most model files do not: on vLLM main (checked 2026-08-17)
**86 of 131** model files that construct one omit `quant_config`, including
qwen3_5.py, qwen3_next.py, minicpm.py and mixtral.py. `llama.py`, `gemma4.py`,
`qwen2.py`, `qwen3_moe.py` and `deepseek_v2.py` pass it, which is why quantized
embeddings appeared to work -- every architecture they had been tried on happened
to be in the passing third.

The consequences are silent in the worst direction. A *tied* EXL3 model keeps its
dense fp16 embedding and loses the whole saving with no error at all. A checkpoint
carrying the block-quantized embedding of `vllm_exl3_plugin/blockq.py` fails to
load, complaining that `embed_tokens.bq_q` does not exist -- which points nowhere
near the cause.

Rather than patch 86 model files, default the config from the one being built
under. `get_current_vllm_config()` is already how `linear.py` and
`logits_processor.py` read ambient construction state, so this is the established
idiom rather than a new mechanism.

**This does not change behavior for configs that do not quantize embeddings**:
they return None from `get_quant_method` for a VocabParallelEmbedding and land on
`UnquantizedEmbeddingMethod` exactly as before. Verified on this box: AWQ on
qwen3_5 (the same architecture the fix unblocks) still gets
UnquantizedEmbeddingMethod and a dense 1940 MiB embedding, bitsandbytes on
Qwen3-0.6B likewise, and the plugin's own end-to-end suite (tied Llama and gemma4,
both of which already passed quant_config) is unchanged. With it, Qwen3.5-9B
serves its embedding from 549 MiB instead of 1940.

Worth upstreaming rather than carrying: any out-of-tree quantization plugin that
serves embeddings hits this, and `vllm-gguf-plugin`'s GGUFEmbeddingMethod is
equally unreachable on those 86 architectures today.

**Reported upstream 2026-08-28 as
[vllm-project/vllm#54304](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/54304)**, with
an llm-compressor reproduction, the root cause, and why *this* fix is unsatisfying —
deliberately as an issue and not a PR, because choosing between defaulting from
ambient config and threading `quant_config` through 86 model files is a maintainer's
call, not ours. Someone volunteered to pick it up. **So check the issue before
re-applying this at the next bump**: whatever lands upstream may not resemble what is
below, and re-applying on top of a different fix is the failure mode to avoid.

diff --git a/vllm/model_executor/layers/vocab_parallel_embedding.py b/vllm/model_executor/layers/vocab_parallel_embedding.py
index 6eed2b5249..3a6e23e06b 100644
--- a/vllm/model_executor/layers/vocab_parallel_embedding.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/layers/vocab_parallel_embedding.py
@@ -281,6 +281,20 @@ class VocabParallelEmbedding(PluggableLayer):
         )
         self.embedding_dim = embedding_dim
 
+        # Most model files never pass `quant_config` here (86 of 131 that build a
+        # VocabParallelEmbedding omit it), so a quantization method that serves
+        # embeddings is simply unreachable on those architectures. Fall back to the
+        # config being built under, the way linear.py and logits_processor.py already
+        # read ambient state. Configs that do not quantize embeddings return None from
+        # get_quant_method and land on UnquantizedEmbeddingMethod exactly as before.
+        if quant_config is None:
+            from vllm.config import get_current_vllm_config
+
+            try:
+                quant_config = get_current_vllm_config().quant_config
+            except Exception:
+                quant_config = None
+
         quant_method = None
         if quant_config is not None:
             quant_method = quant_config.get_quant_method(self, prefix=prefix)
